    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_e6773e833604e77f8f039a6eb95205d9ca73014d6298203997c3b54f5450987d",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source factors the Lemma 2.1 target into A_x R(M_x) >= exp(gamma), where A_x is exp(2/sqrt(x)) times the finite Euler product through x. Splitting the full Euler product at x and applying the tail bound controls A_x relative to zeta(2), while substituting the primorial M_x into the Dedekind-psi normalization makes R(M_x) tend to exp(gamma)/zeta(2). The constants are complementary, but their product limit is exactly the boundary being sought; without one-sided or rate control on R(M_x), convergence alone does not force the eventual lower inequality asserted in the main proof.",
